## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses practical grounding in per-tenant configuration management, feature flags, and safe deployment strategies for Azure developers.

## Key Concepts

- Azure App Configuration feature flags with tenant-specific overrides
- Cosmos DB partitioning by tenantId for logical tenant isolation
- Canary deployments using GitHub Actions with environment promotion gates
- Secrets governance via Azure Key Vault integration

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal example: fetch a tenant flag from App Configuration
const { AzureAppConfigurationClient } = require('@azure/app-configuration');

const connectionString = process.env.APPCONFIG_CONNECTION_STRING;
const client = new AzureAppConfigurationClient(connectionString);

async function getTenantFlag(tenantId, flagKey) {
  const tenantOverrideKey = `featureFlags/${tenantId}/${flagKey}`;
  const defaultKey = `featureFlags/default/${flagKey}`;

  try {
    const tenantSetting = await client.getSetting(tenantOverrideKey);
    return tenantSetting.value === 'true';
  } catch {
    const defaultSetting = await client.getSetting(defaultKey);
    return defaultSetting.value === 'true';
  }
}
```

